#Create Development Workspace
 Create a new folder for the project. 
 Create a Python virtual environment. 
 Activate the virtual environment. 
 Install Django. 
 Install Django REST Framework. 
 Install PostgreSQL driver. 
 Install python-dotenv. 



Create Enterprise Django Project
 Create a new Django project. 
 Understand every generated file. 
 Explain the purpose of: 
  manage.py
  settings.py
  urls.py
 Run the development server. 
 Verify the Django welcome page. 


Configure PostgreSQL Database
 Install PostgreSQL. 
 Create a new database. 
 Create a database user. 
 Grant permissions. 
 Configure Django to connect to PostgreSQL. 
 Run initial migrations. 
 Verify all default tables are created. 


Understand Django Project Architecture
  Create the following application structure:
   core
   accounts
   common
 Learn why large projects are divided into apps.
 Document the purpose of each app.


Configure Environment Variables
  Create a .env file.
Move:
 Secret Key 
 Database Name 
 Username 
 Password 
 Host 
 Port 
 Update settings to read values from .env.
 Verify the application still runs.


Configure Django REST Framework (1 Hour)
 Install DRF. 
 Add DRF to Installed Apps. 
 Create first API endpoint. 
 Return JSON response. 
 Understand Request and Response objects. 
 Test using browser 
 

Create Custom User Model (1.5 Hours)
  Research:
  Why create Custom User before migrations? 
  Implement:
   Custom User model 
   Email login 
   UUID Primary Key 
   Required fields 
   Run migrations.
  Verify database tables. 